@scene chapter_3_endless_bridge

background: forest_gate.png
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"Beyond the Gate of Choices, the forest thins."
"The Old Man's gift still warms your hands — the power to decide, freely given."
"But the path does not run far before it simply... stops."

background: valley_vista.jpg

dialogue:
"The ground falls away into a chasm so deep its bottom is only a rumour."
"On the far side, half-lost in drifting mist, the path resumes."
"Between the two edges: nothing. No bridge. Only a single weathered pillar at the cliff's lip, carved with instructions worn almost smooth."

npc You:
"There's no way across."

dialogue:
"As you speak, the air near the pillar curdles."
"A stain the colour of a healed-over wound clings to the stone — the same wrongness the System has warned of."
"The Blight. Where it touches, things forget how to work."
"Here, it has devoured the bridge itself."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE ENDLESS BRIDGE"
"Build a path across the Blighted chasm."

dialogue:
"Far across the divide, you can just make out a figure."
"A man in a warden's cloak, pacing — three steps forward, three steps back — along the same short stretch of stone."
"He never gets anywhere. He never stops."
"You call out. He does not seem to hear."

npc System:
"The bridge was not broken, Traveller. It was UNMADE."
"It has forgotten how to repeat itself."
"A bridge is only one plank — laid again, and again, and again, until it reaches the other side."

dialogue:
"The pillar's carvings flare to life."

npc System:
"To repeat an action is to LOOP."
"Name a count — from one, up to the width of the gap."
"And for each number in that count, lay a single plank."
"Speak the loop, and the bridge will build itself, plank by numbered plank."

dialogue:
"The System sets the width of the chasm: a number, n."
"You must lay a plank for every step from 1 to n — in order, none skipped, none repeated."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Loop from 1 to n. Lay each plank, in order, into the bridge."

mission: loops_intro

dialogue:
"You speak the loop."
"A plank of light snaps into being at your feet — the first."
"Then the second, laid on the echo of the first. Then the third."
"The bridge unrolls itself across the chasm, one plank for every count, until it kisses the far edge."
"You cross."

background: deep_forest.jpg

dialogue:
"On the far side, the pacing warden still walks his three steps, back and forth, trapped in a loop that never learned to end."
"He watches you pass with hollow, envious eyes."

background: warden

npc Warden:
"You gave your loop a place to STOP, traveller."
"I never did. Mine has no way out."
"...Remember me, when someone finally teaches you the word 'break'."

dialogue:
"You want to help him. But you do not yet know how."
"Not yet."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Endless Bridge"
"Applied: for loops · range · building a sequence"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 40
achievement: BRIDGE-BUILDER

next:
chapter_3b_echoing_halls
